{"title":"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the numerical coefficients of all the terms in the expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24c4c5b536e63db77ef13c777b1a8dca6f957ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2y)^{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3218d3af50d8b4be1c0fcd48005fd1b7ebe9c7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 19\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ -1\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ -19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"411\" height=\"17\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any polynomial, even a polynomial with more than one variable, the sum of all the coefficients (including the constant, which is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83ba2dd9c548b9e51656853c0d04ae5c16a7a42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^0y^0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />) is found by setting all variables equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Note that we don't have to worry about whether a constant is a coefficient of an \"invisible\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83ba2dd9c548b9e51656853c0d04ae5c16a7a42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^0y^0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> term, because there is no such term here.\n</p><p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915f1781caa8b3e0eddafe7a445019f06178da22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03efbfb6a45793a7cb481ac5a240c2589b11fa46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"19\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME\" title=\"1964 AHSME\">1964 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1964 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class